instruction:
Repo: /echo (Go, module github.com/labstack/echo/v4, echo v4.2.1 source). Fix a bug in /echo/context.go in `func (c *context) Scheme() string`.

Expected behaviour (from the hidden test `TestContext_Scheme` and its subtests `ignores invalid X-Forwarded-Proto and uses X-Forwarded-Protocol` and `ignores invalid forwarded headers and falls back to http`): Scheme() must never return an arbitrary/garbage header value. The doc comment on `Context.Scheme()` says: "Scheme returns the HTTP protocol scheme, `http` or `https`." So a forwarded header value that is not a valid scheme (e.g. "invalid") must be IGNORED, and the code must continue with the next header, finally falling back to "http".

Implement exactly this (keep the existing comment lines and structure, gofmt-clean tabs):

func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}

Do NOT change anything else in the repository. Do NOT touch any *_test.go file permanently.

Verification (run and report exact output):
1. `cd /echo && gofmt -l context.go` (must print nothing)
2. `cd /echo && go build ./...`
3. `cd /echo && go test ./... -count=1 2>&1 | tail -20` (everything must still pass)
4. Create TEMPORARY file /echo/context_zz_tmp_test.go (package echo) containing a test that checks: (a) TLS -> "https"; (b) X-Forwarded-Proto "https" -> "https"; (c) X-Forwarded-Proto "invalid" + X-Forwarded-Protocol "https" -> "https"; (d) all four forwarded headers set to "invalid" -> "http"; (e) X-Forwarded-Proto "invalid" + X-Forwarded-Ssl "on" -> "https"; (f) X-Forwarded-Protocol "http" -> "http"; (g) X-Url-Scheme "https" -> "https". Use the internal `&context{request: &http.Request{...}}` form like the existing TestContext_Scheme in context_test.go. Run `cd /echo && go test ./ -run 'TmpScheme' -v` and report output.
5. DELETE the temp file, then `cd /echo && git status --porcelain` must show ONLY ` M context.go` (plus possibly ` M middleware/proxy.go` which is a pre-existing change you must not touch).

Report: the git diff of context.go, output of every command, and confirmation the temp test file is deleted.
